From: ShadowOfTheVOID <126734193+ShadowOfTheVOID@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Counter plugins: a drop-in folder and --add-plugin

Adding a counter meant editing config/vision.yaml (plugin_paths:) or
pip-installing a repo. Now:

- vision/plugins/my_counter.py: a class with a NAME is available as
  counter: <NAME>. Files are read with ast, never imported, so a broken
  plugin cannot stop vision from starting or break --list-counters.
- python run_vision.py --add-plugin ~/dev/YOLOv26-FRC-Model records the
  folder as vision/plugins/<repo>.path (one line of text; no symlink, so
  it works on Windows) and prints the counter names it provides.
  --remove-plugin <repo> undoes it. A .path to a moved folder is listed
  as missing, not fatal.
- vision/plugins/_example.py: a working template with every optional
  part commented. Built-in names still cannot be taken over.

Verified with the YOLOv26-FRC-Model repo: --add-plugin found
tbavid-colour / tbavid-combo and both load; the copied template counts.
5 new tests; 42 pass.

